  This gate has a row that writes into crates/ and restores it with
  `git checkout --`. Until 2026-08-10 it ran on trees like this one and
  the restore ate the edit: board #2668 (a lane re-applied work the gate
  discarded) and board #2907 (a lane shipped, then retracted, a claim made
  from a run that graded the pre-edit tree while printing the post-edit
  commit). The row is fixed; this refusal is the part that does not depend
  on any row staying fixed.

  Commit or stash, then re-run — a gate run is evidence about the tree it
  graded, and uncommitted work has no name to put on that evidence.
  If you truly mean to grade an uncommitted tree, pass
  --allow-dirty-crates: the run proceeds, says so on every headline, and
  the row that would rewrite crates/ is refused instead of run.
